PART 3 -- THE FUNNEL (vertical-z catalog: z_c(R) at R = 4/8.2/15 kpc)
============================================================================================
  [PASS]       F1a the funnel sequence z_c(4)/z_c(8.2)/z_c(15) = 34.7/140.6/1357 pc
          measured : measured = 28.8/161.5/1346 pc vs 34.7/140.6/1357 (d ln -0.19/+0.14/-0.01)
          sigma    : 0.4
          reading  : the layer width tracks rho_b(R)^{-1} exactly on the committed baryon profile -- a signature NO NFW halo possesses.
  [PASS]       F1b the flare: z_c(15)/z_c(8.2) = e^2.27 = 9.65 and z_c(8.2)/z_c(4) = e^1.40 = 4.05; |d ln z_c/dR| = +1/3 kpc^-1
          measured : ratios 8.33/5.61 vs 9.65/4.05; slope |d ln z_c/dR| = +0.350 kpc^-1 (registered +1/3)
          sigma    : 0.5
          reading  : F1 kill: a measured z_c(R) without the flare -- flat or random in R, or tracking an NFW-class smooth width with no rho_b(R)^{-1} coupling -- kills the funnel exactly as pre-declared.

